From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:03:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Hide the VT-d superpages with the IGD too

Document 492662 sets SPCAPCTRL in ARCHDIS of the remapping engine for
the devices other than the IGD only when the IGD is absent. With the
IGD present the engine then reports 2 MiB and 1 GiB superpages, and
Linux prints "dmar1: ... cap d2008c20660462".

The vendor firmware of Haswell machines hides them: in the Linux logs
of linux-hardware.org, about 1200 logs of the Lenovo ThinkPad T440p,
W540 and W541, Dell Latitude E6440, E6540 and E7440, Precision M4800
and M6800, OptiPlex 7020 and 9020, HP EliteBook 840 G1, ZBook 15 and
17 and Apple MacBookPro11,1 to 11,3 all have "cap d2008020660462".

Where the superpages are shown, Linux maps 2 MiB pages that the engine
rejects: DMA faults with reason 0x0c, "non-zero reserved fields in
PTE", on a 2 MiB-aligned address and on 4 KiB pages inside it, and the
transfer is lost. On a ThinkPad W541 with Linux 7.2 and intel_iommu=on
these were SATA reads, which btrfs found as blocks of zeros. The same
faults show up on a MacBookPro11,5, whose firmware also reports the
superpages (from its GPU, with Linux 5.15), and on a Z97 board, where
intel_iommu=sp_off made them go away.

Set SPCAPCTRL with the IGD too.

TEST=Build for the ThinkPad W541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
index f58a7b04f..49987a766 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
@@ -174,10 +174,14 @@ static void northbridge_setup_iommu(void)
 
 		clrsetbits32p(VTVC0_BASE_ADDRESS + 0xf04, 0xf << 15, 1 << 15);
 
-		u32 vtvc0_archdis = 0x000a5003 | DMAR_LCKDN;
-		if (pci_read_config16(PCI_DEV(0, 2, 0), PCI_DEVICE_ID) == 0xffff) {
-			vtvc0_archdis |= SPCAPCTRL;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * The document sets SPCAPCTRL, which hides the superpages of
+		 * this engine, only without the IGD. The vendor firmware of
+		 * Haswell laptops and desktops hides them with the IGD too,
+		 * and where they are shown Linux gets DMA faults "non-zero
+		 * reserved fields in PTE" on the 2 MiB pages it maps.
+		 */
+		const u32 vtvc0_archdis = 0x000a5003 | SPCAPCTRL | DMAR_LCKDN;
 		write32p(VTVC0_BASE_ADDRESS + ARCHDIS, vtvc0_archdis);
 	}
 	if (cpu_is_broadwell()) {
